  "notes": "Census read from the vendor's own Port Layout table: https://techspecs.ui.com/unifi/cloud-gateways/ef-core (HTTP 200, 674,322 B, server-rendered, read 2026-11-19) prints six rows - \"1 GbE RJ45 = 2 (1G/100M/10M)\", \"10 GbE RJ45 = 8 (10G/5G/2.5G/1G/100M)\", \"25G SFP28 = 4 (25G/10G/1G)\", \"100G QSFP28 = 4 (100G/40G)\", \"MGMT = 1 (1G/100M/10M)\", \"Console = 1\". Before this correction the row carried only the first two of those and no management or console socket, so a 1U firewall that ships with both had 18 jacks where the unit has 20. The management port is a separate RJ45 on the front panel, not one of the two 1 GbE data ports: the vendor lists it as its own row with its own rate set, and the same table's Management section reads \"Ethernet\" alongside the 1.3\" LCM touchscreen. Both 1 GbE data ports also gain the 10M rung the vendor prints for them. Power, unchanged and confirmed on the same page: \"Max. Power Consumption = 171W\", \"Power Method = Universal AC input, 100-240V AC, 7.5A Max., 50/60 Hz\", \"Power Supply = (2) Hot-Swappable AC/DC 550W PSU\" - no PoE front end, so every copper port here is a plain socket."
